{"y":2020,"label":"2019–20","coach":"Dan Hurley","conf":"AAC","confShort":"AAC","w":19,"l":12,"cw":10,"cl":8,"confFinish":"5th in AAC","finish":"none","srs":11.15,"sos":5.34,"ortg":102.3,"drtg":94.1,"pace":69.0,"ppg":72.8,"oppg":67.0,"story":{"headline":"\"Better Get Us Now\"","text":"UConn's farewell season in the American brought freshman James Bouknight, a redshirt year for Howard transfer R.J. Cole, and signs of life: a win over No. 15 Florida at Gampel, a double-overtime loss to No. 18 Xavier in the Charleston Classic, Bouknight's 23 points in a 72–71 overtime win over Cincinnati, and a 77–71 senior-night win over No. 21 Houston. After a January loss at Villanova, Dan Hurley warned opponents that they had \"better get us now\" — because it was coming. Bouknight made third-team All-AAC, and UConn went 19–12 and 10–8, its first winning season since 2015–16. The Huskies were set to face Tulane in the AAC tournament on March 12, 2020, when the COVID-19 pandemic canceled the event hours before tipoff.","moments":[{"date":"2020-03-12","title":"Season canceled","text":"The AAC tournament is canceled hours before UConn's game against Tulane as the COVID-19 pandemic spreads."}],"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2019%E2%80%9320_UConn_Huskies_men's_basketball_team","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UConn_Huskies_men%27s_basketball","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Bouknight","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christian_Vital"]},"roster":[{"pid":"christian-vital-1","name":"Christian Vital","num":"1","cls":"SR","pos":"G","ht":"6-2","wt":187,"home":"Queens Village, NY","hs":"St. Thomas More Prep","photo":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/headshots/mens-college-basketball/players/full/4066443.png","photoStudio":true,"pg":{"g":31,"gs":31,"mp":32.2,"pts":16.4,"trb":6.3,"ast":2.6,"stl":2.5,"blk":0.2,"tov":2.7,"fg_pct":0.398,"fg3_pct":0.346,"ft_pct":0.899,"orb":1.3,"pf":2.6},"tot":{"mp":998,"fg":154,"fga":387,"fg3":66,"fg3a":191,"ft":133,"fta":148,"orb":39,"drb":156,"trb":195,"ast":8